Hero stats are separated into several different factors

The first is the seeded random generation from summoning

The characters base stats are distributed by their potential

Character potential ratings 
| Name           | Rarity / 1000    | Growth Bonus |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Celestial Hero |    1 -   1 (001) | 1.0          |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Demigod Hero   |    2 -   3 (002) | 0.83         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Ascendant Hero |    4 -   7 (004) | 0.68         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Mythical Hero  |    8 -  15 (008) | 0.54         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Legendary Hero |   16 -  31 (016) | 0.42         |   
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Renowned Hero  |   32 -  63 (032) | 0.32         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Epic Hero      |   64 - 127 (064) | 0.25         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Notable Hero   |  128 - 255 (128) | 0.18         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Uncommon Hero  |  256 - 511 (256) | 0.13         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|
| Common Hero    |  512 - 1024 (512)| 0.10         |
|----------------|------------------|--------------|


Each level the hero will gain previous_stat  

So while their base stats are flat, they will eventually grow to very high levels


The growth of a character is equal to this equation

L = Level
I = Initial Stat (1 - 10)
M - Max Stat Value (65536)
X = Max Level (250)
P = Potential (0-1)

New Stat (L) = (I / 10) * M * (1 - (1 - (L / X) ^^ (1 + 4*P)))

